      "writtenOn": "2023-04-01T06:12:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What about having `kTexture` be marked with SkUNREACHABLE and remove the `default` case entirely. The compiler will then warn about additional types that are added later?\n\u003e \n\nDone. I kept the `SK_ABORT` for the texture case to display an error message.\n\n\u003e Although I suppose we aren\u0027t handling the uniform buffer type right now, but IIUC, its use case fits very closely with the kTexture being populated externally, right?\n\nCorrect, though I think I want to support uniform bindings with the internal mechanism as well, perhaps with a `ComputeStep::prepareUniformBuffer` method that is passed a `UniformWriter`. Currently I wanted to support both internal and external resource allocation as that provides more flexibility.\n\nFWIW, while implementing the vello renderer I found external allocation and explicit assignment of all resources generally convenient (so the same vello render function can allocate and assign resources in one place). I expect the internal allocation mechanism via methods might prove more useful with geometry processing in the existing path renderers. For that use case in particular, I would like to rethink the state machine to better enable batching of geometry data across draws.",
      "parentUuid": "22fbd1ca_a513e6f2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 283,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d70596926c15caf04df526221c49f640daaa34ee",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
